 no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Indiana has been a reliably Republican presidential state, backing the Democratic ticket only once in recent decades, in Barack Obama's 2008 win. Its partisan lean of roughly nine points Republican, combined with Trump-backed candidates sweeping recent statewide races there, points to a Republican advantage in the 2028 open-seat contest. No candidates have been settled and no Indiana polls exist yet, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying lean.\n\nThe 2028 field remains wide open on both sides, with no clear front-runners, which adds uncertainty about the national environment. Even so, a Democratic win would likely require a national swing comparable to 2008. The forecast expects the Republican ticket to carry Indiana by a high-single-digit margin, with meaningful but not overwhelming uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1505, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2049, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2014, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2053, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1986, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2114, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2074, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2042, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2034, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2041, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2055, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1998, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1976, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1915, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.1875, "margin": -9.0},